| David Hofmeier, Giovanna Pimenta, Weiguang Cao, *Lattice Gauging Interfaces and Noninvertible Defects in Higher Dimensions*, arXiv:2605.12601v2 (updated 2026-08-04), INSPIRE 3155176 with no DOI/journal record at this query. | Retrieved 45-page PDF; inspected abstract/introduction PDF pp. 1–5 and conclusion pp. 33–34. The abstract claims explicit \(\mathbb Z_2^{(0)}\) gauging interfaces in 2+1D and \(\mathbb Z_2^{(1)}\) interfaces in 3+1D lattice models, plus movement operators and subgroup-gauging examples. Those are concrete model-specific results under source assumptions, not a general higher-dimensional gauging theorem; the paper’s full construction was not independently reviewed here. |
