given by\n\n$$\nb_{ij}=g_i a_{ij}g_j^{-1},\\qquad \\zeta^g_{ijk}(a)=-\\beta(g_i,a_{ij},a_{jk})+\\beta(b_{ij},g_j,a_{jk})-\\beta(b_{ij},b_{jk},g_k),\\qquad C=\\rho_gB+\\zeta^g(a)+\\delta_b\\lambda.\n$$\n\nRaw pairs remain distinct even when their induced functions on backgrounds coincide. For fixed $g$ and target edge labels $b$, a $2$-arrow $t:(g,\\lambda)\\Rightarrow(g,\\lambda')$ is a vertex $A$-cochain satisfying $\\lambda'-\\lambda=\\delta_b t$. There are no $2$-arrows between different vertex labels $g$. Vertical composition adds vertex cochains; the identity $2$-arrow is zero.\n\nFor consecutive $1$-arrows $(g,\\lambda):x\\to y$ and $(h,\\mu):y\\to z$, write $a,b,c$ for the successive edge labels. Their composite is $(hg,\\nu)$, where\n\n$$\n\\nu_{ij}=\\rho_{h_i}\\lambda_{ij}+\\mu_{ij}+\\tau(h,g;a)_{ij},\\qquad \\tau(h,g;a)_{ij}=\\beta(h_i,g_i,a_{ij})-\\beta(h_i,b_{ij},g_j)+\\beta(c_{ij},h_j,g_j).\n$$\n\nHorizontal composition of $t$ on the first arrow and $s$ on the second is $s+\\rho_h t$. Identity $1$-arrows have all vertex labels $e$ and edge labels zero. For three consecutive arrows $g,h,k$, the associator from $((k\\circ h)\\circ g)$ to $k\\circ(h\\circ g)$ is the vertex cochain $\\sigma_i=\\beta(k_i,h_i,g_i)$. Unit constraints are identity $2$-arrows.\n\nA $2$-groupoid here means these data form a bicategory: each pair of objects has a category of $1$-arrows and $2$-arrows; horizontal composition preserves identities and vertical composition; associators are natural and obey the pentagon; units obey the triangle identity; all $2$-arrows are invertible and every $1$-arrow has a reverse up to invertible $2$-arrows. Finiteness means all three sets of labels are finite. Coherence of the displayed data is a separate theorem.\n\nWrite $\\pi_0\\mathcal B(K)$ for the equivalence classes of objects under $1$-arrows. For an object $x$, let $\\pi_1(\\mathcal B(K),x)$ be the group of $2$-isomorphism classes of $1$-automorphisms of $x$, and let $\\pi_2(\\mathcal B(K),x)$ be the abelian group of $2$-automorphisms of its identity $1$-arrow. In particular, $\\pi_2$ retains vertex cochains with $\\delta_a t=0$ rather than discarding them. For a subcomplex $L\\subseteq K$ and fixed background $s$ on $L$, the **relative background 2-groupoid** has objects restricting exactly to $s$, $1$-arrows with $g=e$ on vertices of $L$ and $\\lambda=0$ on edges of $L$, and $2$-arrows with $t=0$ on vertices of $L$.","design_state":"Step 1 authored; owner round-two supplier/consumer repair complete, native readiness rehash remains owner-owned.","inventory_expansion_required":false},{"id":"thm-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid-coherence","kind":"theorem","domain":"mathematics","title":"Coherence and stabilizers of finite background gauge 2-groupoids","dependency_level":3,"deps":["def-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid","thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency"],"dependency_roles":{"def-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid":"mathematical-premise","thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency":"mathematical-premise"},"provenance":{"statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated"},"sources":{"references":[{"title":"Baez and Lauda, Higher-Dimensional Algebra V: 2-Groups","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0307200","locator":"§8.3 pp.55–63; associator cocycle p.59 and monoidal coherence pp.60–61; explicit finite cochain 2-groupoid constructed locally."},{"title":"Benini, Cordova and Hsin, On 2-Group Global Symmetries and Their Anomalies","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1803.09336","locator":"§2.3, printed pp.18–20 / PDF19–21; background and gauge equations only, explicit coherence reconstructed locally."}]},"library":"mathematics","proof_strategy":"direct","reference":"items/thm-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid-coherence.md","statement":"For every finite ordered simplicial complex and finite data $(G,A,\\rho,\\beta)$ in the background gauge $2$-groupoid definition, its displayed operations define a finite $2$-groupoid, including the relative version for 