The linear map depends on interpolating spacetime and the stuff that happened in between.
In QFT, Fampl is often computed from a path integral, and indeed, the axioms for Fampl
below are intended to capture properties one expects such path integrals to satisfy. Most
path integrals of interest are extremely difficult to compute. It can be helpful to extract or
axiomatize key properties of path integrals. In topological quantum field theory (TQFT),
we axiomatize to retain the key properties of locality.
Topological field theory (TFT) is meant to capture this very basic idea in a way that
expresses locality but eliminates almost all the complications of typical quantum systems.
Accordingly in TFT, we take as axiomatic that the values of Fstates and Fampl only depend
(up to a suitable notion of isomorphism) on the diffeomorphism class of N 0
n−1, N 1
n−1, and
Mn, respectively.
The axiomatic definition for TFT we will give below turns out to define an amazingly rich
mathematical structure, one that continues to be explored and refined in current research.
Moreover, it naturally suggests a formulation of field theory in general. This formulation,
sometimes known as geometrical field theory or functorial field theory is discussed briefly in
Section 27. One of the main motivating examples is G. Segal’s formulation of 2d conformal
field theory (CFT) [Seg02]. Giving a fully satisfactory definition of quantum field theory
along such lines is an extremely ambitious goal for the future. Somewhat surpris
