It turns out that we can equip manifolds with topological and geometrical structures
and still define bordism groups. One simple example is orientation. Another is (s)pin
structure.
So there are also oriented bordism groups, (s)pin bordism groups, etc.
Bordism groups play an especially important role in the application of TFT to the
mathematical theory of topological phases of matter.

