of Morse-Cerf theory.
Recall that a Morse function on a manifold Mn is a smooth real-valued function on Mn
that has isolated nondegenerate critical points. A critical point p ∈Mn is a point where
df(p) = 0. The associated critical value is f(p). A critical point is called nondegenerate if
the Hessian at p, defined to be
