Some Background On Categories

The structure we have encountered is precisely that of a category. The formal definition
of a category is given in Section 8. Comparing with the definition given there, we see that
for 2d open-closed TFT, there is a category C of boundary conditions whose set of objects
C0 is the set of boundary conditions, labeled a, b, c, . . . , and whose hom spaces Hom(a, b)
are the vector spaces of open string states Oab. The composition in the category is the
multiplication provided by the pair of chaps in Figure 22.

Figure 22: Multiplication.

A natural question arises as to the analog of a Frobenius algebra structure and the sewing
theorem (cf. Theorem 6.1) for the open-closed case. This was provided in [MS06, Sec. 2.2].
The proof of the sewing theorem (in Appendix A.2 of that paper) again makes use of Morse
theory, but now for manifolds with boundary. A general formulation of Morse theory for
manifolds with boundary has been discussed in [KM07, Sec 2.4], and in [BNR12].

