Now, VECT is a tensor category, using the tensor product of vector spaces. The associator
is trivial, so this is a symmetric tensor category. Less trivially, the category of super-vector
spaces is also a symmetric tensor category.
Moreover Bord⟨n−1,n⟩is a symmetric tensor
category where the monoidal structure is defined using the disjoint union.16

