as a description of the long-distance, low-energy physics of the anyonic excitations. General
ideas of low energy effective theory predict that the low-energy physics of a gapped system
that breaks parity symmetry should be described by some Chern-Simons theory (which has
only one derivative in the action). Chern-Simons theory turns out to be particularly well-
suited to fractional quantum Hall systems.18 In this description, anyons can be “fused” and
the mathematical embodiment of that is to model anyons as objects in a braided tensor
category. In general, for anyons, Ωy,x ◦Ωx,y is not the identity.
The “fusion of the anyons” can be pictured as:

