|S(Y )| →Y induces an isomorphism of homotopy groups, and when Y is a CW complex
(see footnote 22), the map is a homotopy equivalence. Thus, in homotopy theory, we may
pass freely between simplicial sets to topological spaces.
Finally, given a group G, we form the simplicial set X(G) and take its geometric real-
ization to form a concrete model for BG:

BG = |X(G)| .
(15.25)

Note that if G is a topological group, X(G) is not the same simplicial set as S(G).

