Example 3: Spin Theories. Theories that involve fermions typically require a choice of
spin or spinc structure on the spacetime. A simple example is supersymmetric quantum
mechanics, where the dynamical fields are maps of a (1|1) supermanifold29 to a Riemannian
target space (X, gX). The partition function on the circle depends on the choice of spin

