further discussion.) Once again, the field should be viewed in terms of a sheaf valued in
simplicial sets, for the same reason as for gauge theories – locality. However, in this case, it
is even more important to do so because of the phenomena of “ghosts for ghosts” in theories
of higher-form fields. One can take the nerve of that (higher) groupoid and that is the value
of F(Mn).

