A crucial property of an H-group is that if X is a pointed space, then the set of basepoint
preserving homotopy classes of maps [X, P] is a group. Conversely, if P is a space with
basepoint such that the sets [X, P] admit a group structure for all based spaces X, then P
is an H-space. A key example of an H-space is the based loop space ΩX of a pointed space
X. One can generalize the notion of a principal fiber bundle with group G to a fibration by
H-spaces. The Eilenberg-Maclane spaces are H-spaces, so fibrations by Eilenberg-Maclane
spaces are generalizations of principal bundles. One can show that38

