of the theory on Nn−1 is morally something like L2(XNn−1). States would be derived from
normalizable wavefunctionals Ψ[ϕ(x)] for ϕ ∈X Nn−1. In the TFT setting, with target space
X, the fields are only considered up to homotopy and so our Hilbert space should consist of
wavefunctions defined on the set of homotopy classes of maps Nn−1 →X. If X is a π-finite
space and Nn−1 is closed, the set of homotopy classes of maps will be a finite set and the
Hilbert space will be finite dimensional.44 The set of homotopy classes of “sigma model field
configurations” is just π0(X Nn−1), and so we have the definition of the statespace:

