23.3
Statespaces And Amplitudes For The Finite Homotopy Sigma
Models

The data needed to define a finite homotopy sigma model consists of:

1. A nonnegative integer n, the spacetime dimension.

2. A π-finite space X. (See Section 23.1.)

3. A cocycle λ ∈Zn(X; C×).43

43The isomorphism class of the theory only depends on the cohomology class of λ.

